# Licensing

This repository uses three licenses, selected by material type:

- Software, tests, manifests, and automation: MIT
- Skill instructions, references, and documentation: CC BY-SA 4.0
- Synthetic sample data: CC0 1.0

The complete, unmodified license texts are in `LICENSES/`. The machine-readable
path-to-license mapping is in `REUSE.toml`; SPDX headers on Python runtime files
remain valid when those files are copied independently.

## Required attribution for documentation

When sharing or adapting CC BY-SA 4.0 material, preserve this notice or provide
equivalent attribution:

> “Professional Kanban skill” by Liz Rettig and contributors, ProKanban.org,
> licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Derived in part from *The Kanban Guide* (May 2025)
> by Orderly Disruption Limited and Daniel S. Vacanti, Inc., licensed under
> CC BY-SA 4.0. Additional sources are listed in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Indicate material changes and license adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 as required.

## Trademarks

These licenses grant copyright permissions only. They do not grant rights in the
ProKanban.org name, logo, Professional Kanban Trainer (PKT), or related
certification marks.

